## B2 executor B knows nothing of A: the identity is put again, and a start needs the bytes (no shared object store)
```json
{
  "putB": {
    "outcome": "created",
    "home": "/tmp/m-h5-77014/homes-b/vera-lund",
    "epoch": 0
  },
  "homeRef alone": "invalid_request: champion.start: home object e3249e531f3fc049374ebc63dcfa77d644978a5898d5eaccbe16b6d0b878c733 is not in the object store /tmp/m-h5-77014/objects-b; hand it over as homeBytes",
  "bytes that do not hash to homeRef": "champion_fenced: champion.start: handover epoch 0 is older than this node's epoch 1 for vera-lund",
  "homeBytes without homeRef/epoch": "invalid_request: champion.start: homeBytes needs homeRef and epoch (the handover from the executor that owned the home)",
  "homeTreeBefore": {
    "MEMORY.md": "d7870cdadd1ac3b4"
  }
}
```
